('10a1-w10-p172-q20',$question_json${"id":"10a1-w10-p172-q20","classroom":"10A1","examWeek":10,"exam":"10A1 · 10th week practice","topic":"Use the Pythagorean Theorem and its converse","type":"MCQ","marks":1,"difficulty":"Standard","diagram":"none","image":"","prompt":"Can $\\sqrt5,\\sqrt{12},\\sqrt{13}$ be the side lengths of a triangle? If so, classify it as acute, obtuse, or right.","promptAr":"هل يمكن أن تكون $\\sqrt5,\\sqrt{12},\\sqrt{13}$ أطوال أضلاع مثلث؟ إذا كان ممكناً، فصنّفه إلى حاد أو منفرج أو قائم.","answer":"The triangle inequality holds. Compare squares: $5+12>13$. The triangle is acute.","answerAr":"تتحقق متباينة المثلث. وبمقارنة المربعات: $5+12>13$؛ لذا فهو مثلث حاد الزوايا.","options":["Obtuse triangle","Not a triangle","Acute triangle","Right triangle"],"optionsAr":["مثلث منفرج الزاوية","لا تشكل مثلثاً","مثلث حاد الزوايا","مثلث قائم الزاوية"],"sourcePage":172,"sourceQuestion":20,"triangleClassification":{"sides":[2.23606797749979,3.4641016151377544,3.605551275463989],"choiceValues":["obtuse","not-triangle","acute","right"]},"correctIndex":2}$question_json$::jsonb),
